ow tucks back the queen. It has done its job pressuring Black's king, so now it's time to defend the c2-pawn.} 10.Qd1 10...c6 {Black attacks our bishop.} 11.Be4 {We'll retreat to e4, keeping its activity. White has a comfortable position — pawn up and ongoing pressure against Black's weakened pawn. We'll continue with moves like d3 to continue developing and castling to hide our king and bring the rook into the game.} *

